      "sourceTextSha256": "39a674b93ee875db388766efd340aa061bcc01fdb6f7ae7fdb081bfea067644d",
      "text": "About 12 nautical miles off the Osa Peninsula, Caño Island is a biological reserve of geographical and archaeological importance, whose true beauty lies underwater. Its clear blue waters, among the bluest in the country, are home to coral reefs and a remarkable variety of marine life: Caño Island is one of the finest diving spots in Costa Rica, where sea turtles, dolphins, rays, moray eels, barracudas, tuna, snapper and grouper are often seen, as well as reef sharks and, in season, humpback whales. (B, L, D)",
